WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.327
Open WebUI is a web interface for interacting with local and remote AI models.

00:00:05.327 --> 00:00:17.485
It gives users a familiar chat-based workspace where they can ask questions, compare models, manage conversations, upload supporting material, and organize AI-assisted workflows.

00:00:17.485 --> 00:00:28.345
In a homelab, small team, or private AI environment, it often becomes the visible layer that turns model infrastructure into something people can actually use.

00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:33.058
It is important to separate the web interface from the model runtime.

00:00:33.058 --> 00:00:35.380
A runtime loads and serves models.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:45.352
A web UI provides the user-facing experience: accounts, conversations, settings, prompts, document workflows, model selection, and administration.

00:00:45.352 --> 00:00:55.187
Open WebUI may connect to local inference services, remote APIs, or OpenAI-compatible endpoints at a high level, but it is not the model itself.

00:00:55.187 --> 00:01:01.266
A web UI adds usability and workflow structure, but it also adds administration concerns.

00:01:01.266 --> 00:01:03.178
Conversations may be stored.

00:01:03.178 --> 00:01:06.867
Uploaded files may become part of knowledge workflows.

00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:09.394
Users may have different permissions.

00:01:09.394 --> 00:01:13.355
Endpoint credentials may be configured in the application.

00:01:13.355 --> 00:01:18.136
Logs, backups, and browser access can all carry sensitive information.

00:01:18.136 --> 00:01:23.600
A chat interface feels simple, but it sits on top of real systems and real data.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.630
Avoid the assumption that local automatically means secure.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:41.495
A local or private AI stack can improve privacy compared with sending everything to a public service, but only if access is controlled, deployment choices are deliberate, and data handling is understood.

00:01:41.495 --> 00:01:48.803
Open WebUI is most useful when it is treated as a manageable AI workspace, not just a convenient front end.
